//calc_bars_count = 3024 (12 years of 252 bars/year) - no need for more

//@version=6
indicator("Minervini VCP (perf sweep)", overlay = true, calc_bars_count = 12 * 252, max_bars_back = 500)

import drebel/DRELib/39 as drelib
import drebel/DREPerf/27 as dreperf

// ============================================================================================
// DESIGN NOTES - Minervini VCP (Volatility Contraction Pattern)
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source: docs/trading/Minevrini/Minervini-strategy.md (in the yt repository), sections 6 and 10.
// This block describes the IDEA and which parts of the document are implemented. It deliberately
// avoids the parameter values of the rows below - those are the sweep, not the definition.
//
// WHAT A VCP IS (section 10.1-10.3)
//   A base inside an existing Stage-2 uptrend, made of two to six progressively smaller pullbacks.
//   Volume dries up through the contractions, the final contraction is tight and quiet, and the
//   stock breaks above the pivot (the high of the final contraction) on expanding volume. The
//   pattern is a supply/demand story: each pullback removes weaker holders, so the final breakout
//   needs little demand to move the price.
//
// TREND TEMPLATE (section 6.1) - the qualifier, not the trigger
//   Eight criteria, simple moving averages, no EMA substitution:
//     1. close > SMA150 and close > SMA200
//     2. SMA150 > SMA200
//     3. SMA200 rising (vs 22 sessions ago)
//     4. SMA50 > SMA150 and SMA50 > SMA200
//     5. close > SMA50
//     6. close >= 1.30 x 52-week low
//     7. close >= 0.75 x 52-week high
//     8. relative strength rank >= 70
//   Criterion 8 is the hard one to compute on a single-symbol chart: a true RS rank is
//   cross-sectional (percentile against the whole universe). This script offers three proxies and
//   the sweep measures which one carries the edge:
//     rsLine  - close/benchmark above its own 100-session average (the ETSB house proxy),
//     rsPct   - percentile (0..100) of a weighted 3/6/9/12-month relative return against its own
//               1-year history (the section 6.3 formula, self-ranked),
//     rs80    - the same percentile with an 80 threshold.
//   None of them is IBD's proprietary ranking; treat them as approximations.
//
// BASE DETECTION - confirmed swing pivots, no repainting (section 10.11)
//   Pivots are 3-bar fractals (left = right = 3), so a pivot is only visible three bars after it
//   happened. Pivots closer than 2% to the previous opposite pivot are dropped (noise filter).
//   The base start is the most recent confirmed swing high that is (a) at least 10 and at most 180
//   sessions old and (b) not more than 2% below the highest high of the last 180 sessions. From
//   that high the code walks the alternating pivot list and records every high -> low leg as one
//   contraction. The last six contractions are kept (Minervini: 2-6).
//   The pivot is the high of the LAST contraction; the stop reference is its low. The final
//   contraction may still be forming - the breakout trigger is what turns "forming" into a signal.
//
//   Simplifications, stated explicitly:
//     - the base start is anchored to the 180-session high instead of an unbounded scan,
//     - the contraction list is shared by all rows; a row's base-length parameter is a GATE on
//       the measured base, not a re-detection with a different window,
//     - the G9 "down-leg volume < up-leg volume" clause is approximated by a 60-session
//       down-volume / up-volume ratio (per-contraction volume means are not reconstructed).
//
// HARD GATES OF THE CANONICAL ROW (section 10.4, G1-G13)
//   G1 Stage 2 (trend template), G2 prior advance >= 30%, G3 base 15-90 sessions, G4 2-6
//   contractions, G5 monotonic contraction, G6 final depth <= 10%, G7 base depth <= 40%, G8 higher
//   lows >= 60%, G9 volume dry-up (5d / ADV50) <= 0.65 and down/up volume <= 1.0, G10 last 10-day
//   range / pivot <= 10% and ATR5/ATR20 <= 0.70, G11 overhead <= 3%, G12 close/pivot <= 1.05,
//   G13 RS >= 70. G14 (fundamentals) and G17 (earnings blackout) are NOT implemented: the scan
//   runs on daily OHLCV only and the corpus has no point-in-time fundamentals feed. G15 (market
//   regime) is approximated by DRELib's wide-index + sector modifier. G16 (liquidity) is the
//   DRELib general filter with the ADR floor disabled, because the VCP family tested in this
//   repository is a "quiet" family and an ADR floor hurt it (see variants/ITERATIONS.md).
//
// ENTRY (section 10.6)
//   Standard breakout: close above pivot x (1 + buffer), volume >= multiple x ADV, and close not
//   more than maxChase above the pivot (do not chase an extended move). Alternative entries are
//   tested as separate rows: anticipation / "cheat" (buy the upper half of the final contraction
//   before the pivot breaks), two-day confirmation (close in the upper 40% of the bar and above
//   the previous high), and failed-breakout reclaim (undercut of the final low within five
//   sessions, then a close back above the pivot).
//
// STOP AND OUTCOME MODEL (section 10.7, DREPerf)
//   DREPerf evaluates a signal at the close of the signal bar and checks a fixed window of bars.
//   "Success" = the stop is not violated inside the window; the return is measured at the end of
//   the window, or at the stop when it was hit. Two stop models:
//     structural - max( min(finalLow x 0.995, close x 0.97), close x 0.92 ), i.e. just below the
//                  final contraction low, at least 3% and never more than 8% below the entry
//                  (section 10.7 verbatim),
//     house      - max(lowest(low, 3), close x 0.92), the convention used by ETSB and by every
//                  previous analysis in this repository, kept for comparability.
//   The table reports win%, N, avgR, PF, maxDD, score, sumWinR and sumLossR - the schema consumed
//   by scripts/tv_table_scraper.py.
//
// VARIANT NAMING
//   vcpCanon  - the canonical row (all gates of section 10.4 at their documented values)
//   vcpC3/4   - minimum number of contractions
//   vcpF6/8/12- max final contraction depth [%]
//   vcpR85/95 - max ratio "current depth / previous depth" (0.99 = strictly decreasing)
//   vcpR100   - non-increasing depth (ratio 1.00)
//   vcpDry50/Off - volume dry-up threshold (5d / ADV50)
//   vcpVol20  - breakout volume multiple 2.0
//   vcpVol30Ma- volume reference = 30-session average instead of 50
//   vcpBaseDepth30 - max base depth 30%
//   vcpPrior20/50  - min prior advance 20% / 50%
//   vcpBase60/120  - max base length 60 / 120 sessions
//   vcpOh5/10      - max overhead above the pivot 5% / 10%
//   vcpTight6      - last 10-day range <= 6% of the pivot
//   vcpAtr60       - ATR5/ATR20 <= 0.60
//   vcpHl80        - higher-lows ratio >= 80%
//   vcpTtOff/Light/House - trend gate: none / MA stack only / DRELib Minervini template
//   vcpRsOff/Line/80     - RS gate: none / RS line above SMA100 / self-percentile >= 80
//   vcpRegime0/1   - require a non-bearish / bullish wide-index+sector regime
//   vcpChase3      - max 3% above the pivot
//   vcpCheat       - anticipation entry inside the final contraction
//   vcpFail        - failed-breakout reclaim
//   vcpConfirm     - two-day confirmation entry
//   vcpStopHouse/5 - house stop / structural stop capped at 5%
//   vcpCheck60     - 60-bar outcome window instead of 30
//   vcpFlat        - flat base: one contraction, shallow base, tight range
//   vcpRange       - pure range-contraction breakout, no pivot structure at all
//
// The canonical row is deliberately kept in every iteration as the reference point.
// ============================================================================================

//signal performance check inputs (same defaults as ETSB)
iShowTable = input.bool(defval = true, title = 'Show table', display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iSigCheckTime = input.int(defval = 30, title = 'Signal check time [candles]', minval = 5, maxval = 200, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iSigStopLossMaxPct = input.float(defval = 8.0, title = 'Stop loss [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 20.0, step = 0.5, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigSuccessRate = input.float(defval = 46.0, title = 'Min. sig success rate [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigReturnAdrMultiple = input.float(defval = 1.2, title = 'Min. avg. return by ADR multiple', minval = -1.0, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.05, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigCount = input.int(defval = 30, title = 'min. signals count', minval = 0, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')
iMinSigWilsonLb = input.float(defval = 30.0, title = 'min. win-rate lower bound (Wilson) [pct]', minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, display = display.none, group = 'Sig. performance check')

// ============================================================================================
// SHARED BUILDING BLOCKS (computed once per bar, used by all rows)
// ============================================================================================
adrPct = 100.0 * (ta.sma(high / low, 100) - 1)
adrCond = iMinSigReturnAdrMultiple * adrPct

//trend template ingredients (section 6.1) - simple moving averages on purpose
sma50 = ta.sma(close, 50)
sma150 = ta.sma(close, 150)
sma200 = ta.sma(close, 200)
low52 = ta.lowest(low, 252)
high52 = ta.highest(high, 252)
sma200Rising = sma200 > sma200[22]
ttFull = close > sma50 and close > sma150 and close > sma200 and sma50 > sma150 and sma50 > sma200 and sma150 > sma200 and sma200Rising and close >= 1.30 * low52 and close >= 0.75 * high52
ttLight = close > sma50 and sma50 > sma150 and sma150 > sma200 and sma200Rising
ttHouse = drelib.isMinevriniBullishTrend(true, false, 0.5)

//relative strength proxies (section 6.3 - RS is NOT RSI)
benchClose = drelib.getDefaultBenchmarkClose()
rsLine = benchClose > 0 ? close / benchClose : na
rsLineStrong = rsLine > ta.sma(rsLine, 100)
rsRel63 = nz(close / close[63] - 1.0) - nz(benchClose / benchClose[63] - 1.0)
rsRel126 = nz(close / close[126] - 1.0) - nz(benchClose / benchClose[126] - 1.0)
rsRel189 = nz(close / close[189] - 1.0) - nz(benchClose / benchClose[189] - 1.0)
rsRel252 = nz(close / close[252] - 1.0) - nz(benchClose / benchClose[252] - 1.0)
rsRaw = 0.40 * rsRel63 + 0.20 * rsRel126 + 0.20 * rsRel189 + 0.20 * rsRel252
rsPct = ta.percentrank(rsRaw, 252)

//market regime proxy (section 8): wide index + matching sector, -2..+2
sigMod = drelib.getWideIndexAndSectorSignalMod(31)

//liquidity / price filter: turnover and a sane price band, ADR floor disabled on purpose
generalFilter = drelib.generalFilter(0.2, 0.0, 1.0, 1750.0, 30)

//volume and volatility references
adv30 = ta.sma(volume, 30)
adv50 = ta.sma(volume, 50)
adv100 = ta.sma(volume, 100)
volMa5 = ta.sma(volume, 5)
volDry5 = adv50[1] > 0 ? volMa5[1] / adv50[1] : 1.0 //measured BEFORE the trigger bar
atr20v = ta.atr(20)
atr5v = ta.atr(5)
atrRatio = atr20v[1] > 0 ? atr5v[1] / atr20v[1] : 1.0 //measured BEFORE the trigger bar
downVol = math.sum(close < close[1] ? volume : 0.0, 60)
upVol = math.sum(close >= close[1] ? volume : 0.0, 60)
downUpRatio = upVol > 0 ? downVol / upVol : 10.0
range10 = ta.highest(high, 10)[1] - ta.lowest(low, 10)[1] //final-contraction range, trigger bar excluded
range30Abs = ta.highest(high, 30)[1] - ta.lowest(low, 30)[1]
refHigh180 = ta.highest(high, 180)[1]
priorLow = ta.lowest(low, 180)
closeLoc = high > low ? (close - low) / (high - low) : 0.0
failLow5 = ta.lowest(low, 5)
houseSl = math.max(ta.lowest(low, 3), close * 0.92)
atrSl = math.max(close - 2.0 * atr20v, close * 0.92)

// ============================================================================================
// CONFIRMED SWING PIVOTS (3-bar fractal, 2% noise filter, alternating high/low)
// ============================================================================================
var array<float> pivP = array.new_float()
var array<int> pivB = array.new_int()
var array<int> pivT = array.new_int()

pushPivot(float _price, int _bar, int _type) =>
    int _n = array.size(pivP)
    bool _sameType = _n > 0 and array.get(pivT, _n - 1) == _type
    if _sameType
        //two highs (or two lows) in a row: keep the extreme, drop the other
        bool _better = _type == 1 ? _price > array.get(pivP, _n - 1) : _price < array.get(pivP, _n - 1)
        if _better
            array.set(pivP, _n - 1, _price)
            array.set(pivB, _n - 1, _bar)
    else
        //opposite type: require a minimum swing amplitude and chronological order
        float _lastP = _n > 0 ? array.get(pivP, _n - 1) : na
        bool _bigEnough = na(_lastP) or math.abs(_price / _lastP - 1.0) >= 0.02
        if _bigEnough and (_n == 0 or _bar > array.get(pivB, _n - 1))
            array.push(pivP, _price)
            array.push(pivB, _bar)
            array.push(pivT, _type)
    if array.size(pivP) > 120
        array.shift(pivP)
        array.shift(pivB)
        array.shift(pivT)

float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, 3, 3)
float pl = ta.pivotlow(low, 3, 3)
if not na(ph)
    pushPivot(ph, bar_index - 3, 1)
if not na(pl)
    pushPivot(pl, bar_index - 3, -1)

// ============================================================================================
// BASE AND CONTRACTION STRUCTURE (shared by all rows)
// ============================================================================================
var array<float> cHi = array.new_float()
var array<float> cLo = array.new_float()
var array<int> cHiB = array.new_int()
var array<int> cLoB = array.new_int()
var float baseStartP = na
var int baseStartB = na
var float baseHighV = na
var float baseLowV = na
var int baseBarsV = 0
var float pivotV = na
var float finalLowV = na
var int contrN = 0

array.clear(cHi)
array.clear(cLo)
array.clear(cHiB)
array.clear(cLoB)
baseStartP := na
baseStartB := na
baseHighV := na
baseLowV := na
baseBarsV := 0
pivotV := na
finalLowV := na
contrN := 0

if array.size(pivP) >= 4
    //most recent confirmed high that is not more than 2% below the 180-session high
    int _k = -1
    for _i = 0 to array.size(pivP) - 1
        if array.get(pivT, _i) == 1
            int _b = array.get(pivB, _i)
            int _age = bar_index - _b
            if _age >= 10 and _age <= 180 and array.get(pivP, _i) >= 0.98 * refHigh180
                _k := _i
    if _k >= 0
        float _curH = array.get(pivP, _k)
        int _curHB = array.get(pivB, _k)
        for _j = 0 to array.size(pivP) - 1
            if _j > _k
                if array.get(pivT, _j) == -1
                    array.push(cHi, _curH)
                    array.push(cLo, array.get(pivP, _j))
                    array.push(cHiB, _curHB)
                    array.push(cLoB, array.get(pivB, _j))
                else
                    _curH := array.get(pivP, _j)
                    _curHB := array.get(pivB, _j)
        //keep the six most recent contractions (Minervini: 2-6)
        while array.size(cHi) > 6
            array.shift(cHi)
            array.shift(cLo)
            array.shift(cHiB)
            array.shift(cLoB)
        contrN := array.size(cHi)
        if contrN > 0
            baseStartP := array.get(pivP, _k)
            baseStartB := array.get(pivB, _k)
            baseBarsV := bar_index - baseStartB
            pivotV := array.get(cHi, contrN - 1)
            finalLowV := array.get(cLo, contrN - 1)
            float _bh = array.get(cHi, 0)
            float _bl = array.get(cLo, 0)
            for _m = 0 to contrN - 1
                _bh := math.max(_bh, array.get(cHi, _m))
                _bl := math.min(_bl, array.get(cLo, _m))
            baseHighV := _bh
            baseLowV := _bl

// ============================================================================================
// VARIANT FACTORY
// ============================================================================================
//all thresholds are applied to the shared structure above; the parameters ARE the variant
vcpCalc(simple int _minContr, float _maxFinalDepthPct, float _depthRatio, float _minContrDepthPct, float _maxBaseDepthPct, float _minPriorAdvPct, int _minBaseBars, int _maxBaseBars, float _maxOverheadPct, float _maxFinalRangePct, float _maxAtrRatio, float _maxVolDryup, float _maxDownUpVol, float _breakoutVolMult, float _breakoutMarginPct, float _maxChasePct, simple int _trendMode, simple int _rsMode, int _regimeMin, simple int _entryMode, simple int _stopMode, simple int _volRef, float _higherLowsMin, simple int _debounce) =>
    bool _baseOk = contrN > 0 and not na(pivotV) and not na(baseStartB)
    float _adv = _volRef == 30 ? adv30 : _volRef == 100 ? adv100 : adv50
    float _pivot = nz(pivotV)
    float _finalLow = nz(finalLowV)
    float _baseHigh = nz(baseHighV)
    float _baseLow = nz(baseLowV)
    float _baseDepth = _baseHigh > 0 ? 100.0 * (_baseHigh - _baseLow) / _baseHigh : 100.0
    float _finalDepth = _pivot > 0 ? 100.0 * (_pivot - _finalLow) / _pivot : 100.0
    float _overhead = _pivot > 0 ? 100.0 * (_baseHigh / _pivot - 1.0) : 100.0
    float _finalRange = _pivot > 0 ? 100.0 * range10 / _pivot : 100.0
    float _priorAdv = _pivot > 0 and priorLow > 0 ? 100.0 * (_pivot / priorLow - 1.0) : 0.0
    //contraction progression: every leg must be a real contraction and must not expand
    bool _monoOk = true
    if contrN >= 2
        for _i = 1 to contrN - 1
            float _h0 = array.get(cHi, _i - 1)
            float _h1 = array.get(cHi, _i)
            float _d0 = _h0 > 0 ? 100.0 * (_h0 - array.get(cLo, _i - 1)) / _h0 : 0.0
            float _d1 = _h1 > 0 ? 100.0 * (_h1 - array.get(cLo, _i)) / _h1 : 0.0
            if _d1 > _d0 * _depthRatio
                _monoOk := false
            if _d1 < _minContrDepthPct
                _monoOk := false
    //higher lows: fraction of contractions whose low holds the previous low
    float _hlRatio = 1.0
    if contrN >= 2
        int _hl = 0
        for _i = 1 to contrN - 1
            if array.get(cLo, _i) >= array.get(cLo, _i - 1) * 0.99
                _hl += 1
        _hlRatio := 1.0 * _hl / (contrN - 1)
    bool _structOk = _finalDepth <= _maxFinalDepthPct and _baseDepth <= _maxBaseDepthPct
    bool _trendOk = _trendMode == 0 ? true : _trendMode == 1 ? ttLight : _trendMode == 2 ? ttFull : ttHouse
    bool _rsOk = _rsMode == 0 ? true : _rsMode == 1 ? rsLineStrong : _rsMode == 2 ? rsPct >= 70.0 : rsPct >= 80.0
    bool _regimeOk = sigMod >= _regimeMin
    bool _volOk = _maxVolDryup >= 2.0 ? true : volDry5 <= _maxVolDryup
    bool _duOk = _maxDownUpVol >= 2.0 ? true : downUpRatio <= _maxDownUpVol
    bool _atrOk = _maxAtrRatio >= 2.0 ? true : atrRatio <= _maxAtrRatio
    bool _overheadOk = _overhead <= _maxOverheadPct
    bool _baseLenOk = _baseOk and baseBarsV >= _minBaseBars and baseBarsV <= _maxBaseBars
    bool _priorOk = _priorAdv >= _minPriorAdvPct
    //triggers
    float _trig = _pivot * (1.0 + _breakoutMarginPct / 100.0)
    bool _chaseOk = close <= _pivot * (1.0 + _maxChasePct / 100.0)
    bool _volBreakOk = volume >= _breakoutVolMult * _adv
    bool _breakOk = close > _trig and _chaseOk and _volBreakOk
    bool _cheatOk = close < _pivot and close > _finalLow and _finalDepth <= 14.0 and close >= _finalLow + 0.5 * (_pivot - _finalLow) and volume >= _adv
    bool _failOk = failLow5 < _finalLow * 0.995 and close > _trig and _volBreakOk
    bool _confirmOk = _breakOk and closeLoc >= 0.60 and close > high[1]
    bool _entryOk = _entryMode == 0 ? _breakOk : _entryMode == 1 ? _cheatOk : _entryMode == 2 ? _confirmOk : _failOk
    bool _raw = generalFilter and _baseOk and contrN >= _minContr and _monoOk and _hlRatio >= _higherLowsMin and _structOk and _trendOk and _rsOk and _regimeOk and _volOk and _duOk and _atrOk and _overheadOk and _baseLenOk and _priorOk and _finalRange <= _maxFinalRangePct and _entryOk
    float _debSum = math.sum(_raw ? 1.0 : 0.0, _debounce + 1)
    bool _sig = _raw and (_debounce == 0 or _debSum == 1.0)
    float _structSl = math.max(math.min(_finalLow * 0.995, close * 0.97), close * (_stopMode == 2 ? 0.95 : 0.92))
    float _sl = _stopMode == 0 ? houseSl : _stopMode == 3 ? atrSl : _structSl
    [_sig, _sl]


// ============================================================================================
// THE 40 ROWS - ITERATION 1
// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IT0 findings drove this grid: the canonical row fires ~never (ATR5/ATR20 <= 0.70 is not a
// tradeable gate on daily data), the confirmation entry (close in the upper 40% of the bar and
// above the previous high) beat the plain breakout on both markets, dry-up at 0.65 helped while
// "dry-up off" only added noise, and 3 contractions improved quality at a large cost in count.
// IT1 centres on the confirmation entry: one-factor perturbations, then ablations of the core.
// ============================================================================================

//1 vcpCanon
[s01, x01] = vcpCalc(2, 10, 0.99, 2, 40, 30, 15, 90, 3, 10, 0.7, 0.65, 1, 1.4, 1, 5, 2, 2, -1, 0, 1, 50, 0.6, 3)
//2 vcpBase80
[s02, x02] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 0, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//3 vcpCfm
[s03, x03] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//4 vcpCfmC3
[s04, x04] = vcpCalc(3, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//5 vcpCfmDry65
[s05, x05] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.65, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//6 vcpCfmDryOff
[s06, x06] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 2, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//7 vcpCfmVol15
[s07, x07] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.5, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//8 vcpCfmVol20
[s08, x08] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//9 vcpCfmPrior50
[s09, x09] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 50, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//10 vcpCfmTtHouse
[s10, x10] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 3, 0, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//11 vcpCfmRsLine
[s11, x11] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 1, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//12 vcpCfmRs70
[s12, x12] = vcpCalc(2, 12, 1, 1.5, 50, 20, 10, 120, 5, 12, 1, 0.8, 1.2, 1.2, 0.5, 7, 1, 2, -99, 2, 1, 50, 0.5, 3)
//13 vcpCfmRegime1
